@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### login as employee first (run auth-req.http login), then:

### list categories to get a categoryId
GET {{baseUrl}}/meta-api/categories

### create ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Laptop won't turn on",
  "description": "Pressed power button, no lights, tried charger swap.",
  "categoryId": "PASTE_CATEGORY_ID"
}

### list my tickets
GET {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets

### get one ticket
GET {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID

### --- Phase 2: approvals ---

### create a ticket in an approval-required category (login as employee first)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Need a second monitor",
  "description": "Requesting a second monitor for my desk.",
  "categoryId": "PASTE_NEW_HARDWARE_REQUEST_CATEGORY_ID"
}

### login as manager (run auth-req.http with manager@sdp.test), then list pending approvals
GET {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets?status=PENDING_APPROVAL

### approve it
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 1
}

### ...or reject it (note is required)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "note": "Please use the shared spare-monitor pool instead.",
  "version": 1
}

### list technicians in your team (manager/admin only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/team-technicians

### put an in-progress ticket on hold (login as the assigned technician)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/hold
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "note": "Waiting on a replacement part from the vendor.",
  "version": 1
}

### resume it
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/resume
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 1
}

### reassign to a different technician (manager/admin)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/reassign
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "technicianId": "PASTE_OTHER_TECHNICIAN_ID",
  "version": 1
}

### --- Phase 3: SLA engine ---

### create a ticket, then immediately downgrade it to the fast "TEST" priority
### to watch it go on-track -> at-risk -> breached in ~1-3 minutes instead
### of waiting on real business hours (login as manager first)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/priority
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "priority": "TEST",
  "version": 1
}

### fetch the ticket a few times over the next few minutes — the "sla"
### object's responseDueAt/resolutionDueAt/warnAt will already be in the
### past, and each fetch triggers the lazy SLA check (see evaluateSla.js)
GET {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID

### check notifications arrived (login as the manager/technician who
### should have been notified)
GET {{baseUrl}}/notification-api/my-notifications

### admin: view/update org-wide business hours
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin-api/org-settings

### admin: e.g. shift business hours to 08:00-20:00
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin-api/org-settings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessHours": { "start": "08:00", "end": "20:00" }
}

### admin: create a policy with businessHoursOnly explicitly set
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin-api/sla-policies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "priority": "URGENT",
  "label": "Urgent",
  "level": 5,
  "color": "#dc2626",
  "responseTimeHours": 0.5,
  "resolutionTimeHours": 2,
  "businessHoursOnly": true
}

### --- SECURE-CORE: the rest of the lifecycle (all need "version") ---
### Read the current version from GET /tickets/:id before every transition.

### manager: assign an OPEN ticket in your team
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/assign
Content-Type: application/json

{ "technicianId": "PASTE_TECHNICIAN_ID", "version": 1 }

### technician: claim an OPEN ticket in your department
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 1 }

### technician (assignee): start / resolve
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 2 }

###
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/resolve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 3 }

### employee (requester): confirm, or reopen with a note
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 4 }

###
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/reopen
Content-Type: application/json

{ "note": "Still broken after the fix.", "version": 4 }

### employee: cancel own ticket (note required)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "note": "No longer needed.", "version": 1 }

### comment (add "isInternal": true as staff; an Employee never sees internal ones)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Checked the charger, port looks damaged.", "isInternal": true }

### --- SECURE-CORE: negative cases ---

### no version -> 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### stale version -> 409 (also what the loser of two simultaneous claims gets)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 999 }

### wrong role: an Employee trying to claim -> 403
### (login as employee@sdp.test first)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 1 }

### wrong team: manager of another department assigning -> 403 (Admin bypass removed too:
### an Admin must assign a technician who belongs to the ticket's department)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/assign
Content-Type: application/json

{ "technicianId": "PASTE_TECHNICIAN_FROM_OTHER_DEPARTMENT", "version": 1 }

### unknown priority -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Bad priority",
  "description": "Priority must match an active SLA policy.",
  "categoryId": "PASTE_CATEGORY_ID",
  "priority": "BANANA"
}

### TEST (level 0) priority as an Employee -> 403 (Admin only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Try the fast SLA",
  "description": "Employees cannot pick the TEST priority.",
  "categoryId": "PASTE_CATEGORY_ID",
  "priority": "TEST"
}

### paging clamp: limit=0 -> 20 (default); limit=500 -> 50; page=-1 -> 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets?limit=0
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets?limit=500&page=-1

### array filters are ignored (no Mongo operator injection)
GET {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets?status[$ne]=CLOSED&priority[]=HIGH

### staff with no department see nothing: login as such a user -> items: [], total: 0
GET {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets

### employee: list/detail/PATCH responses never contain internal comments
GET {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID

### --- TICKET-COMPLETION ---

### CSAT: only the requester, only when the ticket is CLOSED and was confirmed (login as employee)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/csat
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 4, "comment": "Fixed quickly, thanks." }

### rating must be a whole number 1-5 -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/csat
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 6 }

### a second rating for the same closure -> 409; after reopen + close again a new rating overwrites
### someone else's ticket -> 404; ticket not closed yet -> 400

### comment rules:
###  - public reply: requester, assigned technician, team manager, admin
###  - another technician of the team: internal notes only ("isInternal": true), public -> 403
###  - CLOSED / CANCELLED / REJECTED ticket -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Please try the new charger.", "isInternal": false }

### after confirm the ticket has closeReason CONFIRMED and closedAt; reopen clears both
GET {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID
